{
 "about": "The tool calls one real Claude session made for the prompt below, through scripts/mcp_openshape3d.py only (captured with OS3D_MCP_LOG, 2026-09-17). ai_flowerpot.py replays them at narration pace.",
 "model": "claude-opus-5[1m]",
 "prompt": "Design a flowerpot I can 3D print, in the openshape3d app that's open on my iPad. About 110 mm across the top and 100 mm tall, tapered sides, 3 mm walls, a drainage hole in the bottom, and a matching saucer to sit under it. Round over the rim so it's comfortable to pick up. Make it look like terracotta. Check that both parts are valid solids, then export each one as its own STL, ready for my slicer.",
 "durationSeconds": 72.7,
 "turns": 25,
 "reply": "The flowerpot and saucer are built in your open design (\"Untitled 5\"). Both passed the solid check, and each is exported as its own STL.\n\n**Flowerpot**\n- 110 mm across the top, 84 mm at the base, 100 mm tall.\n- The walls are 3 mm thick, measured square to the tapered side. The bottom is also 3 mm.\n- There's a 12 mm drainage hole in the middle of the bottom.\n- Both edges of the rim are rounded with a 1.4 mm radius, so the top edge is fully rounded.\n\n**Saucer**\n- 116 mm across the top, 104 mm at the base, 18 mm tall.\n- The walls and base are 3 mm thick, and the rim is rounded the same way.\n- The flat inside floor is about 100 mm wide, so the pot's 84 mm base sits in it with room to spare.\n- It sits beside the pot in the design.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Volumes:** the pot's volume before rounding (103,429 mm\u00b3) matched my hand calculation, and the saucer's (42,036 mm\u00b3) matched my estimate. After rounding, the pot is 103,133 mm\u00b3 and the saucer is 41,659 mm\u00b3.\n- **Solid check:** with the self-intersection pass on, both came back valid. Each is one closed solid with no problems found.\n- **Colour:** both parts are a terracotta orange-red. I also hid the two sketch outlines so they don't show over the parts in the viewport.\n\n**Files** (millimetres, Z up, so they stand flat on the slicer bed)\n- `out/claude/flowerpot.stl` (30,020 triangles)\n- `out/claude/saucer.stl` (27,172 triangles)\n\nThe export tool reported writing both files, but I couldn't list that folder myself because it's outside what I'm allowed to access, so check they're there.\n\nNeither part should need supports: the pot's sides lean about 7\u00b0 and the saucer's about 18\u00b0. The terracotta colour only shows in the app, since STL files don't store colour, so print with a terracotta-coloured filament to get the look.",
